1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,888
A CrestApps AI assistant is described by a profile, can take its character

2
00:00:05,888 --> 00:00:09,065
from a persona, and can start from a template.

3
00:00:09,065 --> 00:00:13,464
This video shows why they exist, how they fit together, and how to

4
00:00:13,464 --> 00:00:16,580
create, edit and reuse each one in the admin.

5
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:24,097
An AI assistant is more than a model.

6
00:00:24,097 --> 00:00:29,252
It needs instructions, a name and a voice, knowledge to draw on, tools

7
00:00:29,252 --> 00:00:32,440
it may use, and limits that keep it safe.

8
00:00:33,190 --> 00:00:38,341
If those choices were scattered across every chat, widget and workflow, the same

9
00:00:38,341 --> 00:00:44,210
settings would be repeated everywhere, and each team would build its assistants differently.

10
00:00:44,960 --> 00:00:48,038
A profile gathers all of it for one job.

11
00:00:48,038 --> 00:00:55,400
A persona is a reusable character, and templates are reusable starting points and reusable instructions.

12
00:00:56,150 --> 00:01:02,178
You describe an assistant once, reuse the parts that repeat, and change them in one place.

13
00:01:02,178 --> 00:01:06,950
Everything that talks to the AI then runs on the same, approved setup.

14
00:01:11,150 --> 00:01:18,875
A profile is one assistant or task, with its own instructions, model, knowledge, tools and limits.

15
00:01:18,875 --> 00:01:26,080
Chats, chat widgets, text and phone conversations, and workflow tasks all run on a profile.

16
00:01:26,830 --> 00:01:28,737
A persona answers who:

17
00:01:28,737 --> 00:01:33,438
the assistant's name, personality, language, voice and picture.

18
00:01:33,438 --> 00:01:39,910
A profile links to a persona, so changing the persona changes every profile that uses it.

19
00:01:40,660 --> 00:01:43,705
A profile template answers where to start.

20
00:01:43,705 --> 00:01:48,020
It carries ready-made settings, and a new profile copies them.

21
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:51,890
After that, the profile no longer follows the template.

22
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:57,320
A prompt template is a reusable piece of instructions, such as a company

23
00:01:57,320 --> 00:02:00,200
tone, that you add to any profile or chat.

24
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:03,800
Together, these parts keep your assistants consistent.

25
00:02:08,020 --> 00:02:10,789
Open Artificial Intelligence, Profiles.

26
00:02:10,789 --> 00:02:14,481
The list is empty until you create your first profile.

27
00:02:14,481 --> 00:02:18,050
Click Add Profile to open the New AI Profile picker.

28
00:02:18,502 --> 00:02:22,449
Blank profile opens the full editor with nothing filled in.

29
00:02:22,449 --> 00:02:27,488
Every other card is a ready-made starting point, with a description, the kind

30
00:02:27,488 --> 00:02:30,402
of profile it creates, and a Start button.

31
00:02:30,856 --> 00:02:35,447
Choose a category on the left to narrow the cards, or type in Filter.

32
00:02:35,447 --> 00:02:39,855
Here, Talk to people shows the assistants that chat with visitors.

33
00:02:39,855 --> 00:02:41,876
All shows everything again.

34
00:02:42,327 --> 00:02:46,126
A card that is greyed out needs a feature that is not turned on.

35
00:02:46,126 --> 00:02:50,197
It names the feature, so you can ask your administrator to enable it.

36
00:02:50,801 --> 00:02:53,091
Click Start on Website assistant.

37
00:02:53,091 --> 00:02:57,318
The setup step asks for a Title, a Technical name that follows the

38
00:02:57,318 --> 00:02:59,491
title, and the Chat deployment.

39
00:02:59,985 --> 00:03:03,854
Leave the Chat deployment on Default to use the model chosen in the

40
00:03:03,854 --> 00:03:06,345
site settings, then click Create profile.

41
00:03:10,087 --> 00:03:13,980
The profile is saved at once and opens in the full editor.

42
00:03:13,980 --> 00:03:19,517
Everything below is optional, so you can chat with it right away and refine it later.

43
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:26,767
The editor groups settings into cards.

44
00:03:26,767 --> 00:03:31,753
General holds the Title, the Technical name, and the Profile type:

45
00:03:31,753 --> 00:03:35,700
Chat, Utility, Template generated prompt, or Agent.

46
00:03:36,164 --> 00:03:40,859
For a chat profile, the Welcome message greets people in an empty chat.

47
00:03:40,859 --> 00:03:47,444
Turn on Start the conversation automatically, and the assistant speaks first, with an Opening message.

48
00:03:47,898 --> 00:03:52,518
Show on admin menu adds the chat to the Artificial Intelligence menu, so

49
00:03:52,518 --> 00:03:53,999
people can open it.

50
00:03:53,999 --> 00:03:57,138
Title type decides how each chat gets its name.

51
00:03:57,600 --> 00:04:00,776
Deployments and Interactions chooses the models.

52
00:04:00,776 --> 00:04:06,128
The Chat deployment answers the conversation, and the Utility deployment is a smaller

53
00:04:06,128 --> 00:04:07,657
model for side jobs.

54
00:04:07,657 --> 00:04:09,480
Both can stay on Default.

55
00:04:09,932 --> 00:04:12,605
Instructions is the most important card.

56
00:04:12,605 --> 00:04:17,253
The AI persona picks a character, and the System instructions say what the

57
00:04:17,253 --> 00:04:21,029
assistant is, what it should do, and what it must never do.

58
00:04:21,029 --> 00:04:23,062
Write them in plain language.

59
00:04:23,519 --> 00:04:26,386
Parameters fine-tune how the model writes:

60
00:04:26,386 --> 00:04:31,880
the longest answer, the Temperature, and how many Past messages included the assistant

61
00:04:31,880 --> 00:04:33,671
sees with each question.

62
00:04:33,671 --> 00:04:36,239
Leave them empty to use the defaults.

63
00:04:36,693 --> 00:04:41,560
Prompt Security limits how often one person can write, and how many chats

64
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:44,332
someone who is not signed in can start.

65
00:04:44,332 --> 00:04:48,953
Set it for a public assistant; an empty field keeps the site's limit.

66
00:04:49,406 --> 00:04:53,019
The Capabilities tab lets the assistant do more than answer:

67
00:04:53,019 --> 00:04:56,687
it can use tools, call other agents, and reach other systems.

68
00:04:56,687 --> 00:04:59,916
Only roles that are allowed to use a tool can use it.

69
00:05:00,371 --> 00:05:05,182
The Data Processing and Metrics tab decides when an idle chat closes, which

70
00:05:05,182 --> 00:05:09,994
details to pick out of the conversation, and what to analyze after it ends.

71
00:05:09,994 --> 00:05:12,251
Click Save to keep your changes.

72
00:05:16,454 --> 00:05:19,066
Add a second profile from the picker.

73
00:05:19,066 --> 00:05:24,896
Background summarizer creates a Utility profile, which runs in the background, for example

74
00:05:24,896 --> 00:05:27,568
from a workflow, and has no chat page.

75
00:05:27,568 --> 00:05:33,034
Click Create profile to open it in the editor, where the Profile type reads Utility.

76
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:37,453
Back in the list, each profile shows its type as a badge.

77
00:05:37,453 --> 00:05:40,840
Click Actions on a chat profile to work with it.

78
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:46,891
New chat, View chat history and Delete chat history belong to chat profiles.

79
00:05:46,891 --> 00:05:51,120
Utility and agent profiles offer Invoke Profile instead.

80
00:05:51,573 --> 00:05:54,347
Clone starts a new profile from a copy.

81
00:05:54,347 --> 00:05:58,910
It opens unsaved, named Copy of the original, so you check the Title

82
00:05:58,910 --> 00:06:01,993
and the Technical name, and then click Save.

83
00:06:02,449 --> 00:06:06,867
Edit changes a profile, and Delete removes it after you confirm.

84
00:06:06,867 --> 00:06:11,789
To delete several profiles, tick them, and choose Delete above the list.

85
00:06:16,086 --> 00:06:18,760
A persona is a reusable character.

86
00:06:18,760 --> 00:06:23,306
Open Artificial Intelligence, Personas, and click Add Persona.

87
00:06:24,287 --> 00:06:28,719
Give the persona a Title, and a Technical name that profiles link to.

88
00:06:28,719 --> 00:06:32,207
The Description helps editors pick the right persona.

89
00:06:32,665 --> 00:06:37,385
Persona instructions describe who the assistant is and how it talks:

90
00:06:37,385 --> 00:06:39,936
its personality, tone and manners.

91
00:06:39,936 --> 00:06:43,125
Leave the task and the rules to the profile.

92
00:06:43,579 --> 00:06:48,768
Assistant name is the name the assistant uses for itself, and chat screens

93
00:06:48,768 --> 00:06:51,492
show it on the assistant's messages.

94
00:06:51,492 --> 00:06:54,736
Language, Voice and Avatar URL are optional.

95
00:06:54,736 --> 00:06:55,839
Click Save.

96
00:06:56,289 --> 00:07:00,595
To use the persona, open Profiles, and edit a profile.

97
00:07:00,595 --> 00:07:05,833
In the Instructions card, pick the persona in the AI persona field.

98
00:07:05,833 --> 00:07:10,569
Chat interactions and profile templates have the same field.

99
00:07:11,024 --> 00:07:13,575
A persona is linked, not copied.

100
00:07:13,575 --> 00:07:19,014
Edit it once, and every profile that uses it follows from the next message.

101
00:07:23,230 --> 00:07:27,063
Templates save you from setting up the same thing twice.

102
00:07:27,063 --> 00:07:31,390
Open Artificial Intelligence, Templates, and click Add Template.

103
00:07:31,844 --> 00:07:35,011
Available Sources lists the kinds of template.

104
00:07:35,011 --> 00:07:39,517
Profile is a starting point for new profiles, and System Prompt is a

105
00:07:39,517 --> 00:07:41,770
reusable piece of instructions.

106
00:07:41,770 --> 00:07:43,414
Click Add on Profile.

107
00:07:46,684 --> 00:07:50,793
Every template has a Title, a Technical name and a Description.

108
00:07:50,793 --> 00:07:56,152
The Category groups templates in the picker, and Listable offers the template there.

109
00:07:56,152 --> 00:07:59,784
Untick Listable to hide a template without deleting it.

110
00:08:00,242 --> 00:08:02,044
Choose the Profile type.

111
00:08:02,044 --> 00:08:06,548
A profile template has the same cards and tabs as the profile editor,

112
00:08:06,548 --> 00:08:10,392
and whatever you fill in is copied onto every new profile.

113
00:08:10,846 --> 00:08:15,862
In the Instructions card, write the System instructions that all of your assistants

114
00:08:15,862 --> 00:08:20,426
of this kind should follow, such as answering only from approved documents.

115
00:08:20,426 --> 00:08:21,666
Then click Save.

116
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:26,961
The template list has a Create profile button on every profile template.

117
00:08:26,961 --> 00:08:31,740
It opens the same setup step, even for a template that is not listable.

118
00:08:32,191 --> 00:08:37,133
In the New AI Profile picker, the template has its own card, under its category.

119
00:08:37,133 --> 00:08:41,558
A profile keeps no link to its template, so changing the template later

120
00:08:41,558 --> 00:08:44,431
never changes the profiles you already made.

121
00:08:48,628 --> 00:08:52,653
A system prompt template is a reusable piece of instructions.

122
00:08:52,653 --> 00:08:56,018
Click Add Template, and then Add on System Prompt.

123
00:08:56,482 --> 00:08:57,739
Give it a Title.

124
00:08:57,739 --> 00:08:59,794
The Technical name follows it.

125
00:08:59,794 --> 00:09:03,849
Then write the System prompt, which is the text to reuse, such as

126
00:09:03,849 --> 00:09:05,962
a company tone, and click Save.

127
00:09:09,631 --> 00:09:12,496
Now open Profiles, and edit a profile.

128
00:09:12,496 --> 00:09:19,138
In the Instructions card, Prompt templates adds reusable pieces on top of your own instructions.

129
00:09:19,138 --> 00:09:21,221
Click Add prompt template.

130
00:09:28,726 --> 00:09:32,030
The list is grouped by category and has a search box.

131
00:09:32,030 --> 00:09:36,678
It holds your system prompt templates, and the ready-made ones that come with

132
00:09:36,678 --> 00:09:39,142
the site, such as Use Markdown Syntax.

133
00:09:39,142 --> 00:09:40,486
Pick Company tone.

134
00:09:40,937 --> 00:09:46,511
The selected templates are added, in order, before the profile's own instructions.

135
00:09:46,511 --> 00:09:48,601
Remove takes one off again.

136
00:09:48,601 --> 00:09:49,677
Click Save.

137
00:09:53,877 --> 00:09:57,083
A website assistant answers visitors' questions.

138
00:09:57,083 --> 00:10:01,951
Start from the Website assistant card, give it your brand's character with a

139
00:10:01,951 --> 00:10:05,157
persona, and visitors hear one consistent voice.

140
00:10:05,907 --> 00:10:08,506
A company standardizes its assistants.

141
00:10:08,506 --> 00:10:13,467
One profile template holds the approved model, the safety limits and the house

142
00:10:13,467 --> 00:10:17,837
rules, and each team starts from it and adds only its own knowledge.

143
00:10:18,587 --> 00:10:20,951
One persona serves many profiles.

144
00:10:20,951 --> 00:10:26,284
A support assistant and a sales assistant share the same friendly character, while

145
00:10:26,284 --> 00:10:28,647
their rules and knowledge differ.

146
00:10:29,397 --> 00:10:34,002
A Background summarizer is a utility profile that a workflow calls, and an

147
00:10:34,002 --> 00:10:37,685
agent is a specialist that other assistants call for help.

148
00:10:37,685 --> 00:10:39,527
Neither needs a chat page.

149
00:10:41,527 --> 00:10:46,551
A profile describes an assistant, a persona gives it a character, and templates

150
00:10:46,551 --> 00:10:48,561
save you from starting over.

151
00:10:48,561 --> 00:10:50,097
Thanks for watching.

